cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If PyWKSpectra contributes to your research, figures, or publications,
  please cite this software and its author using the information below.
  I would also appreciate hearing about publications that use PyWKSpectra.

type: software

title: "PyWKSpectra: Wheeler–Kiladis Space–Time Spectral Analysis in Python"

authors:
  - given-names: Alejandro
    family-names: Jaramillo-Moreno
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4175-7726"
    email: ajaramillo@atmosfera.unam.mx
    affiliation: >-
      Departamento de Cambio Climático,
      Instituto de Ciencias de la Atmósfera y Cambio Climático,
      Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México (UNAM)

version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23438592"

repository-code: "https://github.com/ajaramillomoreno/PyWKSpectra"
url: "https://github.com/ajaramillomoreno/PyWKSpectra"

license: GPL-3.0-only

abstract: >-
  PyWKSpectra is a Python package for computing symmetric and antisymmetric
  Wheeler–Kiladis space–time power spectra, estimating the spectral
  background, calculating background-normalized spectra, and visualizing
  equatorial-wave dispersion relationships following Matsuno (1966).

keywords:
  - Wheeler–Kiladis
  - space–time spectra
  - equatorial waves
  - tropical atmospheric dynamics
  - spectral analysis
  - Python
